.TH QUANT-FMT 1 "July 2026" "Quant 1.0.0" "Quant Language Tools"
.SH NAME
quant\-fmt \- code formatter for the Quant language
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B quant\-fmt
[\fB\-\-check\fR] [\fIFILE\fR ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B quant\-fmt
formats Quant source files (\fI.qa\fR) according to the canonical Quant
style. It preserves all comments, including comments between top-level
declarations and between statements inside function bodies. Formatting
is idempotent: running it twice produces the same output as running it
once.
.PP
When invoked with no file arguments, \fBquant\-fmt\fR reads from stdin
and writes to stdout, making it composable with editors and shell pipelines.
When given one or more file arguments it formats each file in place.
.PP
.B quant\-fmt
is also wired into the Language Server Protocol as
\fBtextDocument/formatting\fR, so editors with the Quant LSP extension
can invoke it via their built-in format-document command.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-check
Do not modify files. Exit with status 1 if any file would be changed by
formatting, 0 otherwise. Useful in CI to enforce formatting.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
All files are already formatted (or formatting succeeded).
.TP
.B 1
At least one file would be changed (\fB\-\-check\fR mode), or a parse
error prevented formatting.
.SH EXAMPLES
Format a single file in place:
.PP
.RS
.B quant\-fmt src/main.qa
.RE
.PP
Check formatting in CI:
.PP
.RS
.B quant\-fmt \-\-check src/*.qa
.RE
.PP
Format from stdin:
.PP
.RS
.B cat src/main.qa | quant\-fmt
.RE
